{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"Tracker(store:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another "},{"code":"byteBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A segment is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore()"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps every event type declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" in the program’s modules, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library’s own; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore(events:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps only the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" types it lists. Each record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":", part of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":") writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" writes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":" property, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"date in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date]"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date?]"},{"type":"text","text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type of your own or in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types, such as one that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand without being listed, are delivered in this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run but never written, and reported once as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drop is reported on "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": the oldest segments"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set. Call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRDBPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"title":"Stores","anchor":"Stores"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Persistence","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"title":"Persistence","symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/changingevents":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","type":"link","title":"Changing Events","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing Events"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dropReports"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","text":"AsyncQueue"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","text":"DropReport"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"title":"dropReports","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStoreError":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}],"title":"SegmentStoreError","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstoreerror","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" throws: an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument it can’t open a store with, or the file system’s failure."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"title":"Persisting Records","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persisting Records"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","abstract":[{"text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"topic","title":"Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","title":"synchronize()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"synchronize"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","abstract":[{"text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage (","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so it survives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"notPersisted"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A record of the event named "},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" was kept in memory only because its type isn’t one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store’s "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": its records are delivered in this run, but never written, so they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lost if the app ends first. Reported once per type, on its first record, for as long as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store lives; a type left out by mistake is added to "},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"title":"SegmentStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RecordStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/init(events:directory:bytebound:segmentbytecount:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","abstract":[{"text":"A store keeping events of the types ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"directory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; it recovers the records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already there.","type":"text"}],"title":"init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"events","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [any (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP","text":"Event","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7Codablea","text":"Codable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"directory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","text":"FilePath","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byteBound","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segmentByteCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence17SegmentStoreErrorO","text":"SegmentStoreError","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}}}